{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.531,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": "In ∆ABD and ∆CDB, the angles marked with a single arc are equal as they are the opposite angles of a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.161,
            0.531,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "Since AD||BC, and BD is a transversal to it, the angles marked with double arcs are equal as they are alternate angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.545,
            0.087,
            0.829,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.235,
            0.531,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "So, by the AAS condition, the"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.253,
            0.599,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "triangles are congruent, that is, $\\Delta \\mathrm { A B D } \\cong \\Delta \\mathrm { C D B } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.287,
            0.475,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, AD = CB, and AB = CD."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.305,
            0.702,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "Thus, **the opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.339,
            0.562,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "Is it wrong to write $\\Delta  ABD \\cong \\Delta  CBD ?$ Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.365,
            0.849,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": "From these deductions we can find the remaining sides and angles of the parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.401,
            0.728,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.546,
            0.58,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": "Let us list the properties of a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.57,
            0.738,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": "**Property 1:** The opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.595,
            0.757,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": "**Property 2:** The opposite sides of a parallelogram are parallel."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.62,
            0.846,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": "**Property 3:** In a parallelogram, the adjacent angles add up to 180°, and the opposite angles are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.667,
            0.846,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": "？ Are the diagonals of a parallelogram always equal? Check with the parallelogram that you have constructed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.711,
            0.768,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "We see that the diagonals of a parallelogram need not be equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.741,
            0.847,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "？ Do they bisect each other (do they intersect at their midpoints)? Reason and/or experiment to figure this out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.795,
            0.846,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": "**Deduction 8— What is the point of intersection of the two diagonals in a parallelogram?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.844,
            0.848,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": "As in the case of a rectangle, we can find out if the diagonals bisect each other by examining the congruence of $\\Delta \\mathrm { A O E }$ and ∆YOS in the parallelogram EASY."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.915,
            0.12,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": "98"
        },
